 "notes": "AxionPhoton limit from time-domain matched-filter search of MeerKAT (MeerTIME) observation of PSR J2144-3933, converting DM axions to photons in the pulsar magnetosphere. Headline observed limit is Fig. 7 (new_limit_plot.png): 2-sigma upper limit on g_agamma vs axion mass for the fiducial parallax distance D=0.165 kpc, over the mass range 3.9-4.7 ueV, taking the weakest (most conservative) limit within the allowed geometry alpha>20deg, |beta|<4deg. Paper quotes flat g_agamma<5.5e-11 GeV^-1 over this range; the plotted curve fluctuates between ~4.9 and 5.6e-11. Points extracted by pixel analysis of the raster figure (per-column mean of the blue curve, binned to ~60 points), so vertical spikes are smoothed toward ~5.1-5.6e-11. Assumes rho_DM=0.45 GeV/cm^3 (entire halo as axions); no density rescale applied. Factor-of-two in Eq.28 => 2-sigma (~95%) upper limit. Alternative D=0.29 kpc (electron-density models) gives weaker 9.6e-11; not reported here.",
